    },
    {
     "id": "p2",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 5,
     "h": 10,
     "size": "m",
     "html": "<p>A vertical athletic facility organized around a continuous running track that wraps the exterior of the tower. The full circuit, from ground to roof and back, is one mile. Rather than a stack of discrete floors, the building is conceived as a vertical landscape in which circulation becomes the primary program.</p><p>The project treats architecture as a climate-controlled open-air environment. Earth tubes draw outside air through the ground, passively regulating its temperature before it enters the building. Spaces remain open to the air while being thermally moderated, allowing the track and its adjacent programs to operate without full enclosure.</p><p>Along the circuit, the building is experienced through changes in light, exposure and elevation. Shifts in orientation and height continuously alter the runner's relationship to the surrounding city, approximating the conditions of trail running within a vertical structure.</p><p>The ground floor contains the changing rooms, a six-lane pool and the entry to the track. Below grade the condition reverses: the underground levels are largely enclosed, almost cave-like, housing server rooms and saunas.</p><p>Together, these conditions form a vertical sequence of atmospheres, from exposure above to containment below, framing the building as a continuous environmental and spatial experience shaped by climate, movement and time.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Group project with Shu Wei (Josh) Hsu</p><p>2B Design Studio: Environments II</p><p><span>Institution: SCI Arc</span></p><p><span>Instructor: Kordae Henry</span></p>"
    },
